Binds a new vertex array when an OpenGL drawable's index buffer changes. A
drawable bound each segment's vertex array once, with the index buffer it had
then. A symbol bucket replaces its index buffer when a rotation sorts its
overlapping symbols again, and drawables that share an index vector can replace
it for each other, so the vertex array kept drawing with the deleted buffer.
Native drivers then drew the old order. In a browser, Emscripten's WebGL
emulation read the indices from unrelated memory, which scattered symbol
triangles across the map. Each index buffer now has a serial, and a segment
rebinds when the serial it bound no longer matches.
Upstream: not proposed

